  "comment": "The vectors pinning Prima.Identity.RestoreKit, the kit proof cyfr/restore-kit/v1 a person answers a home restored from a backup with: every side derives the recovery key from the seed, re-signs the proof's fields and reproduces its signed JCS bytes and sig byte for byte, reproduces its digest (sha256:<hex> over the JCS bytes of the whole signed proof), and refuses each refused proof with its reason, a decoding refusal naming its field. Binary values are unpadded base64url; the seed is the kit's recovery secret, the Ed25519 private key (RFC 8032). A wrong_signer proof decodes and no recovery key of the head signed it.",
